It is lunchtime.
Now my Saturday work finishes.
I take off my apron.
I look at Sunita.
I say, 'Sunita, thank you for your patience.'
'I am learning to make coffee.'
Sunita smiles.
She says, 'Maya, you did good work today.'
'Your first coffee was not good.'
'But the second coffee was very good.'
I smile, then I go out of the café.
My flat is nearby.
So I walk back home.
Today I am very tired.
But I am very happy.
Because today I learned to do new things.
I served the community here.
I want to come again next Saturday.
